1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://finlander.genealogia.fi/sfhswiki/index.php/Some_Migrating_Families_From_Savo_Village_in_Lappaj%C3%A4rvi_During_the_1600-and_1700s]: The third son Matts Eriksson, born 1705, lived at Barkar with his brother 
2 CONC until 1732, then he moved to the Nix house in Katternö. From Crown administrator Anders Zephrin he received the right to own and use a part of the Nix Crown house in 1732 and became a farmer there as well. He married 1728 to Sofia
2 CONC  Johansdotter Karvala. They had two sons who were farmers at the place.
2 CONT
